-- WRITE-ROUTES-1 (2026-11-04, charter pillar security; roadmap row RM-TP-8-TRUST-BOUNDARY id 133, docs/TRANSFORMATION-PROGRAM.md T8 lever 1; sub-agent c5-resilience of the owner request "CODE, DEPLOY, AND CLOSE ALL OPEN ROADMAP AND BACKLOG TASKS").
-- WHAT WAS MEASURED: T8's exit is "every write route answers 401/403 unauthenticated" and nothing measured it (its other exit, security_open_issues, is not a registered metric). On 2026-11-04 an unauthenticated POST with an empty body to 64 candidate write routes
-- (two censuses, then the collector below over its 15 safe routes) found 12 refusing and 3 open: qnfo-evolve POST /tick answered 200 and ran a whole tick (tickAllowed returned true when LOOP_TOKEN was unset, and that worker holds no secret by design),
-- qnfo-deploy-guard POST /scan answered 200, and qnfo-research-exec POST /run answered 202 and wrote a cloud_ops_events row per call. Reading qnfo-deploy-guard 1.4.6 also shows four writes it cannot probe safely: POST /ledger (forges a fleet_deploys row and
-- ensures a service_registry row for any worker name), POST /thresholds (rewrites the KV cost thresholds the scan grades against; no caller in the repository), POST /lock/acquire (holds any worker deploy lock for up to 7200 s) and POST /capability-snapshot.
-- WHAT THIS DOES: registers unauth_write_routes_open (target 0, producer scripts/bp26_writeroutes.py on the remediation-consumer runner, hourly, over scripts/write-routes.json), its trigger and its cause; files the two open routes this change does not fix as ROADMAP-1 issues with
-- a doer (qnfo-deploy-guard/worker.js is under another session claim, qnfo-research-exec/worker.js under C2-SCOUT); marks T8 lever 2 landed (qnfo-containers-pilot POST /exec answers 403 unauthenticated); sets row 133 partial. qnfo-evolve 0.2.12 closes the first route in the same pull request.
-- APPLY-BY: ci
-- DB: qnfo-audit
-- Rollback: DELETE FROM analytics_metric_triggers WHERE metric_key = 'unauth_write_routes_open'; DELETE FROM metric_breach_cause WHERE metric_key = 'unauth_write_routes_open'; DELETE FROM metric_registry WHERE metric = 'unauth_write_routes_open'; DELETE FROM agent_issues WHERE source = 'session:c5-resilience' AND title LIKE 'ROADMAP-1: QNFO.INFRA WRITE-ROUTES-%'; UPDATE roadmap_implementation SET status = 'not-built', evidence = substr(evidence, 1, instr(evidence, ' || C5-RESILIENCE-133') - 1) WHERE id = 133 AND instr(evidence, ' || C5-RESILIENCE-133') > 0; UPDATE transformation_levers SET status = 'pending', landed_at = NULL, note = 'issue 1677 closed before the lever landed: re-verify by probe' WHERE tp = 8 AND n = 2 AND note LIKE 'C5-RESILIENCE:%';
