INSERT INTO agent_issues (title, description, source, category, priority, status, created_at, updated_at)
SELECT 'ROADMAP-1: QNFO.INFRA WRITE-ROUTES-DEPLOY-GUARD-1: qnfo-deploy-guard POST /scan, /ledger, /thresholds, /lock/acquire and /capability-snapshot answer anonymous callers',
 'QNFO.INFRA; charter pillar security; metric unauth_write_routes_open (the row qnfo-deploy-guard POST /scan reads OPEN in bp26_probe_results; the other four routes are in the register of scripts/write-routes.json marked open-gap because a probe would run them). Read from qnfo-deploy-guard 1.4.6 on 2026-11-04: POST /scan returned HTTP 200 with the scan result to an anonymous caller; POST /ledger inserts a fleet_deploys row and calls ensureRegistry and refreshRegistryVersion for any worker name in the body (ledger forgery and service_registry poisoning); POST /thresholds writes KV guard:cost_thresholds that scan() grades COST-THRESHOLD-BREACH against (an anonymous caller can raise it to silence the anomaly; git grep finds no caller of /thresholds outside this worker); POST /lock/acquire holds the deploy lock of any worker name for up to 7200 s (a stranger can block qnfo-ops deploys); POST /capability-snapshot forces a snapshot. /work-lock/* and /secret-lock/* stay open on purpose: sessions hold no credential (CLAUDE.md). Work: (1) run fleet-graph impact on every DEPLOY_GUARD service binding and git grep the callers of /ledger, /lock/acquire, /lock/release, /scan and /capability-snapshot first (qnfo-ops dg(), qnfo-code-orchestrator, scripts); (2) remove the POST /thresholds writer or put it behind a caller check; (3) for the other four routes accept only a caller that proves it is a fleet worker, with the service-binding props.caller allowlist qnfo-containers-pilot uses (PILOT-PROPS-CALLER-1) or a secret the callers already hold, and answer 403 otherwise; keep GET /scan and the cron path working; (4) add a test that does not depend on live state (anonymous POST to each route answers 403, a binding caller passes); (5) remove the matching open-gap rows from the register in scripts/write-routes.json in the same change. Work claim: file:qnfo-deploy-guard/worker.js was held by D1-observability until 2026-11-05T00:54Z when this was written; take it over when it lapses, or review that change. Prediction: unauth_write_routes_open falls by 1 (the /scan row) and the register no longer lists an open-gap for qnfo-deploy-guard. Closing marker: the change carries the text WRITE-ROUTES-DEPLOY-GUARD-1.' || char(10) ||
 'code-task: repo=qnfo-workers path=qnfo-deploy-guard/worker.js' || char(10) ||
 'code-anchor: async fetch(request, env, ctx) {' || char(10) ||
 'code-probe: {"paths":["qnfo-deploy-guard/worker.js"],"contains":"WRITE-ROUTES-DEPLOY-GUARD-1"}',
 'session:c5-resilience', 'code', 'high', 'open', unixepoch() * 1000, unixepoch() * 1000
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM agent_issues WHERE instr(title, 'ROADMAP-1: QNFO.INFRA WRITE-ROUTES-DEPLOY-GUARD-1:') = 1 AND status = 'open');

